            {
               "text": "### Images from Copan\n\nThese images are copyright for Copan and allowed to be used according to the license determined by them.\n\nTo visualize all images, use the left and right arrows on the slide below.",
               "source": null,
               "date_time": null,
               "isTable": false,
               "imgdesc": "",
               "format": "markdown",
               "PostMention": ""
            },
            {
               "text": "<p><div class=\"htSlides\"><div class=\"htSlide\"><div class=\"htSlideCounter\">1 / 13</div><img class=\"imgGameSize\" id=\"imgCopan0\" onclick=\"htImageZoom('imgCopan0', '0%')\"><div class=\"htSlideCaption\">Altar Q, Copán, Honduras. Detail of the altar depicting kings ( <i>ajawob</i> ). Photo taken on <htdate0>, during a visit to the site (<htcite0>).</div><div class=\"htSlideRefs\"><b>Related content:</b><ul><li>Numerical families (Part II) - We continue exploring our family generations and their connection to numbers. (<htcite1>)</li><li>The result is (Phase II) - a game to reinforce the connection between addition and multiplication. (<htcite2>)</li><li>Translation game (Part I) - Explore numbers from different cultures through an engaging translation game. (<htcite3>)</li><li>The result is - a game of consecutive sums that helps uncover the story. (<htcite4>)</li></ul></div></div><div class=\"htSlide\"><div class=\"htSlideCounter\">2 / 13</div><img class=\"imgGameSize\" id=\"imgCopan1\" onclick=\"htImageZoom('imgCopan1', '0%')\"><div class=\"htSlideCaption\">Altar Q, Copán, Honduras. Detail of the altar depicting kings. Photograph taken on <htdate1>, during a site visit (<htcite5>).</div><div class=\"htSlideRefs\"><b>Related content:</b><ul><li>Numerical families (Part II) - We continue exploring our family generations and their connection to numbers. (<htcite6>)</li><li>The result is (Phase II) - a game to reinforce the connection between addition and multiplication. (<htcite7>)</li><li>Translation game (Part I) - Explore numbers from different cultures through an engaging translation game. (<htcite8>)</li><li>The result is - a game of consecutive sums that helps uncover the story. (<htcite9>)</li></ul></div></div><div class=\"htSlide\"><div class=\"htSlideCounter\">3 / 13</div><img class=\"imgGameSize\" id=\"imgCopan2\" onclick=\"htImageZoom('imgCopan2', '0%')\"><div class=\"htSlideCaption\">Altar Q, Copán, Honduras. Detail of the altar. Photo taken on <htdate2>, during a visit to the site (<htcite10>).</div><div class=\"htSlideRefs\"><b>Related content:</b><ul><li>Numerical families (Part II) - We continue exploring our family generations and their connection to numbers. (<htcite11>)</li><li>The result is (Phase II) - a game to reinforce the connection between addition and multiplication. (<htcite12>)</li><li>Translation game (Part I) - Explore numbers from different cultures through an engaging translation game. (<htcite13>)</li><li>The result is - a game of consecutive sums that helps uncover the story. (<htcite14>)</li></ul></div></div><div class=\"htSlide\"><div class=\"htSlideCounter\">4 / 13</div><img class=\"imgGameSize\" id=\"imgCopan3\" onclick=\"htImageZoom('imgCopan3', '0%')\"><div class=\"htSlideCaption\">Altar Q, Copán, Honduras. Detail of the altar depicting kings. Photograph taken on <htdate3>, during a site visit (<htcite15>).</div><div class=\"htSlideRefs\"><b>Related content:</b><ul><li>Numerical families (Part II) - We continue exploring our family generations and their connection to numbers. (<htcite16>)</li><li>The result is (Phase II) - a game to reinforce the connection between addition and multiplication. (<htcite17>)</li><li>Translation game (Part I) - Explore numbers from different cultures through an engaging translation game. (<htcite18>)</li><li>The result is - a game of consecutive sums that helps uncover the story. (<htcite19>)</li></ul></div></div><div class=\"htSlide\"><div class=\"htSlideCounter\">5 / 13</div><img class=\"imgGameSize\" id=\"CEast\" onclick=\"htImageZoom('CEast', '0%')\"><div class=\"htSlideCaption\">Stela C, east side, Copán, Honduras. Photo taken on <htdate4>, during a site visit (<htcite20>).</div><div class=\"htSlideRefs\"><b>Related content:</b><ul><li>Indigenous (Copan) (<htdate13> - <htdate14>) - In this text, we study the kings (<i>ajawob</i>) of Copan, Honduras. (<htcite21>)</li><li>Same, but different - In this text, we begin to learn how to perform calculations with numbers of opposite signs. (<htcite22>)</li><li>Modulating (Part I) - In this text, we learn that walking in an opposite direction has many things in common with walking in a direction we are used to. (<htcite23>)</li></ul></div></div><div class=\"htSlide\"><div class=\"htSlideCounter\">6 / 13</div><img class=\"imgGameSize\" id=\"CWest\" onclick=\"htImageZoom('CWest', '0%')\"><div class=\"htSlideCaption\">Stela C, detail of the beard, Copán, Honduras. Photo taken on <htdate5>, during a site visit (<htcite24>).</div><div class=\"htSlideRefs\"><b>Related content:</b><ul><li>Indigenous (Copan) (<htdate15> - <htdate16>) - In this text, we study the kings (<i>ajawob</i>) of Copan, Honduras. (<htcite25>)</li><li>Same, but different - In this text, we begin to learn how to perform calculations with numbers of opposite signs. (<htcite26>)</li><li>Modulating (Part I) - In this text, we learn that walking in an opposite direction has many things in common with walking in a direction we are used to. (<htcite27>)</li></ul></div></div><div class=\"htSlide\"><div class=\"htSlideCounter\">7 / 13</div><img class=\"imgGameSize\" id=\"imgCopanWholeTextSA\" onclick=\"htImageZoom('imgCopanWholeTextSA', '0%')\"><div class=\"htSlideCaption\">Structure 10L-26, Hieroglyphic Stairway and surroundings, Copán, Honduras. Photo taken on <htdate6>, during a site visit (<htcite28>).</div><div class=\"htSlideRefs\"><b>Related content:</b><ul><li>Indigenous (Copan) (<htdate17> - <htdate18>) - In this text, we study the kings (<i>ajawob</i>) of Copan, Honduras. (<htcite29>)</li><li>The Writing System - More than just a tool for daily use, the writing system is a milestone that allows us to divide human history into prehistory and recorded events. (<htcite30>)</li><li>Cradles of civilization (Part I) - While humanity originated in Africa, the first civilizations emerged in various regions around the world, such as Mesopotamia, the Andes, and Mesoamerica. (<htcite31>)</li><li>Is this extra? - In this text, we introduce the concept of a remainder in division. (<htcite32>)</li><li>Where Are They? - In this last text of the chapter, we learn where we can find the numbers studied in the whole chapter. (<htcite33>)</li><li>Beyond fingers - Exploring the limitations and the necessity of new tools to count. (<htcite34>)</li></ul></div></div><div class=\"htSlide\"><div class=\"htSlideCounter\">8 / 13</div><img class=\"imgGameSize\" id=\"Copan\" onclick=\"htImageZoom('Copan', '0%')\"><div class=\"htSlideCaption\">Ballcourt in Copán, Honduras. Photo taken on <htdate7>, during a visit to the site (<htcite35>).</div><div class=\"htSlideRefs\"><b>Related content:</b><ul><li>The word - when we combine syllables, we form a word, but what exactly is a word? (<htcite36>)</li><li>What is time? - In this text, we begin to explore one of the most important variables in both history and physics—time. (<htcite37>)</li><li>Understanding the Multiplication Table (8 and 9) - What would happen if we left the plane? And if we went deeper inside? (<htcite38>)</li><li>Anachronism - although it is a word unknown to many, it is an action frequently practiced. (<htcite39>)</li><li>Expanding... - Continuing from the previous text, we see that dividing into just two sides ends up doing omissions (<htcite40>)</li></ul></div></div><div class=\"htSlide\"><div class=\"htSlideCounter\">9 / 13</div><img class=\"imgGameSize\" id=\"imgCopanRosalila\" onclick=\"htImageZoom('imgCopanRosalila', '0%')\"><div class=\"htSlideCaption\">Upper section of Rosalila's full-scale reconstruction, Copán, Honduras. Photograph taken on <htdate8> during a site visit (<htcite41>).</div><div class=\"htSlideRefs\"><b>Related content:</b><ul><li>Indigenous (Copan) (<htdate19> - <htdate20>) - In this text, we study the kings (<i>ajawob</i>) of Copan, Honduras. (<htcite42>)</li></ul></div></div><div class=\"htSlide\"><div class=\"htSlideCounter\">10 / 13</div><img class=\"imgGameSize\" id=\"imgCopanStelaA\" onclick=\"htImageZoom('imgCopanStelaA', '0%')\"><div class=\"htSlideCaption\">Stela A, Copán, Honduras. Photo taken on <htdate9>, during a site visit (<htcite43>).</div><div class=\"htSlideRefs\"><b>Related content:</b><ul><li>Indigenous (Copan) (<htdate21> - <htdate22>) - In this text, we study the kings (<i>ajawob</i>) of Copan, Honduras. (<htcite44>)</li><li>Mesoamerican sums - We studied how the Mesoamericans might have used addition in their numerical system. (<htcite45>)</li><li>Reading and Multiplying - Multiplication helps us navigate a text we are reading. (<htcite46>)</li><li>The four divisions - in addition to the four limbs of the human body, the number four has also been used in various contexts throughout the history of humanity. (<htcite47>)</li><li>Inversion - In life, some experiences yield entirely different outcomes depending on the path we take. Does the same apply to multiplication? (<htcite48>)</li><li>Fractionating Texts - In this text, we delve deeper into the concept of groups and introduce fractions as an additional tool for understanding texts. (<htcite49>)</li><li>Limits and contexts - a common point between science and writing is the fact that people do not always understand their limits. But how can we identify them? (<htcite50>)</li><li>I live on the planet... - It is not only time that has different counts. When we speak of the planet we live on, we also have different ideas about it. (<htcite51>)</li></ul></div></div><div class=\"htSlide\"><div class=\"htSlideCounter\">11 / 13</div><img class=\"imgGameSize\" id=\"imgCopanTemple\" onclick=\"htImageZoom('imgCopanTemple', '0%')\"><div class=\"htSlideCaption\">Temple 16, Copán, Honduras. Photo taken on <htdate10>, during a site visit (<htcite52>).</div><div class=\"htSlideRefs\"><b>Related content:</b><ul><li>Indigenous (Copan) (<htdate23> - <htdate24>) - In this text, we study the kings (<i>ajawob</i>) of Copan, Honduras. (<htcite53>)</li><li>Bigger or Smaller - Concluding the comparisons, we analyze the relationship between objects by classifying them as bigger or smaller. (<htcite54>)</li><li>Learning from nature - This text explores how knowledge of multiplication could have helped ancient civilizations. (<htcite55>)</li><li>Change of direction (Part I) - We study the logic behind the different approach used by indigenous communities as their numbers grow.. (<htcite56>)</li><li>Running Among the Numbers - In this text, we learn how to add large numbers, drawing an analogy to Mesoamerican reconstructions. (<htcite57>)</li></ul></div></div><div class=\"htSlide\"><div class=\"htSlideCounter\">12 / 13</div><img class=\"imgGameSize\" id=\"imgCopanTemple3\" onclick=\"htImageZoom('imgCopanTemple3', '0%')\"><div class=\"htSlideCaption\">Temple 16, external view, Copán, Honduras. Photo taken on <htdate11>, during a site visit (<htcite58>).</div><div class=\"htSlideRefs\"><b>Related content:</b><ul><li>Learning from nature - This text explores how knowledge of multiplication could have helped ancient civilizations. (<htcite59>)</li><li>Building Words with Syllables - In this text, we will explore how to construct words using syllables. (<htcite60>)</li></ul></div></div><div class=\"htSlide\"><div class=\"htSlideCounter\">13 / 13</div><img class=\"imgGameSize\" id=\"imgCopanTempleInside\" onclick=\"htImageZoom('imgCopanTempleInside', '0%')\"><div class=\"htSlideCaption\">Temple 16, interior view, Copán, Honduras. Photo taken on <htdate12>, during a site visit (<htcite61>).</div><div class=\"htSlideRefs\"><b>Related content:</b><ul><li>Learning from nature - This text explores how knowledge of multiplication could have helped ancient civilizations. (<htcite62>)</li><li>Ages and Pyramids - what do a pyramid and the dates of our birthdays have in common? (<htcite63>)</li><li>Running Among the Numbers - In this text, we learn how to add large numbers, drawing an analogy to Mesoamerican reconstructions. (<htcite64>)</li><li>Building Words with Syllables - In this text, we will explore how to construct words using syllables. (<htcite65>)</li></ul></div></div><i class=\"fa-solid fa-chevron-left htSlidePrev\" onclick=\"htPlusDivs(-1);\"></i><i class=\"fa-solid fa-chevron-right htSlideNext\" onclick=\"htPlusDivs(1);\"></i></div></p>",
